            <ArticleTitle>Oxidative functionalisation of alcohols and aldehydes via the merger of oxoammonium cations and photoredox catalysis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>8295-8301</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7ob02243c</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a new paradigm for nitroxyl-mediated processes via the merger of oxoammonium cation-mediated oxidation with visible-light photoredox catalysis. The integration of these two forms of catalysis has been realised for the oxidative amidation of aldehydes, furnishing N-acylated heterocycles. Extension of this process to the oxidative amidation of alcohols via the intermediacy of an aldehyde was successfully pursued, thus proffering a general oxidation platform. The activated amides synthesised here are excellent synthetic handles for acylation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
